<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4086"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Last Trumpet<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 13, 2005 - 3:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What is this that I cannot see <BR>Cold, icy hands taking hold of me <BR>for the Monster has come, you all can see. <BR>Hell has opened it&#39;s gate to trick me. <BR>Oh! Monster, Oh! Monster, can&#39;t you spare me,  <BR>over for another year! <BR>I&#39;ll stuff your jaws till you can&#39;t talk <BR>I&#39;ll bind your leg&#39;s till you can&#39;t walk <BR>I&#39;ll tie your hands till you can&#39;t make a stand. <BR>And finally I&#39;ll close your eyes so you can&#39;t see <BR>I&#39;ll bring all the legions of hell and you&#39;ll never be free. <BR> <BR>But I was a man once and someone&#39;s child <BR>A babyboy all dressed in blue <BR>And there was a time when I once believed <BR>In all the things that were good and true <BR>When I fell from grace, the angels wept <BR>As they beheld the beast that I became <BR>And the lives I stole, the pain I&#39;ve caused <BR>Wears on my soul like a crimson stain <BR>Father, take this cup away from me! <BR>Did He who died for the lost also die for me? <BR> <BR>BTK, what will it be? <BR>Your bonds can be broken, you can make a stand <BR>Your eyes can be opened that you might see <BR>Who will win this victory, the monster or the man? <BR>The price has already been paid to set you free <BR> <BR> <BR>You have been weighed and measured.  The time is at hand. <BR> <BR>Choose.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
