<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4171"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Poetic Justic<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 10:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->For the man known as Btk <BR> <BR> <BR>O Byron! <BR>O Tennyson! <BR>O Keats! <BR>Domiciles now for worms of the deep <BR>In the Twilight  <BR>Hours as you pondered <BR>The reverberating halls of Death  <BR>You wandered <BR>Did your lyrical mind ever conceive <BR>A monster such as me? <BR> <BR>O Byron! <BR>O Tennyson! <BR>O Keats! <BR>Cover me now with a grim refrain <BR>O legend who would Live again <BR>Raise one last toast to our destined feast <BR>Appointed now unto this time <BR>Where breath and flesh shall feed the beast <BR>And through me, the hosts of Hell shall dine<!--/Text--></td></tr>
