<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4174"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->I&#39;m loved<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 15, 2005 - 1:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->All anyone wants is to be loved and to hear the words &#34;I Love you&#34;. BTK you must have someone that does love you, maybe a daughter, a son ? and by now maybe a grandchild or 2. Do they tell you &#34;I love you daddy&#34; or &#34;I love you Grandpa&#34;? How does that make you feel? If I were you and I did the things you did, hearing the words &#34;I love you&#34; would mean nothing to me! For they can&#39;t really love you, because they don&#39;t know the real you! You take peoples lives, leaving others to mourn for the loss of their children or their grandbabies. The next time someone says &#34;I love you&#34; I hope you think about who you really are! If they found out what you&#39;ve done, the things you crave would they still say &#34;I love you?&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
