<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4559"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 3:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Cassanova: Is there any way that you can send Tom a copy of the Otero letter? You need a new typewriter, as the one that you are using sucks eggs. I can decipher some of the letter and am still working on it. Get your just dues, and send copies of your communiques to Tom. We would all appreciate it. After all, the whole world is waiting. By the way, do you like Goldie Hawn?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
