<!--Post: 4661--><!--Time: 1106631046-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elaine Dddvais<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 9:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dude, <BR> <BR>Why did you put the Nancy Fox license and hose inside a see through bag and then place THAT inside a white garbage bag and leave it on the ground in Murdock park? <BR> <BR>What if some idiot had found that, mistaked it for trash and threw it in a public trash can before the RIGHT person found it and turned it in?  What if whoever picked it up had not looked in it and just decided to throw it away?  A garbage bag is really not a good way to disguise good evidence.  <BR> <BR>Got lucky didn&#39;t you and a smart guy found it and turned it in.  Just your luck huh? <BR> <BR>I have an FCC license to operate a radio. Kind of addicting isn&#39;t it?  Trust me I know.  <BR> <BR>Have a good year BTK.  I thank you for not harming anyone else. You have accomplished something if you have stopped hurting people. You are a true hero in your own sense.   <BR> <BR>Next time I&#39;ll share a line from one of my poems for you...about heros.  I think you might like it. Gotta go. <BR> <BR>E <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
