<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4674"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brainstorm<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 6:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Btk, suppose you anonymously gave a profile about yourself.  No one would ever know it was you as everybody and his brother has a profile out there.  And yours would be the one that&#39;s right!  How cool is that?  You could tell a little of your story without really giving anything away.  It would be a way to blow all those &#34;armchair profilers&#34; out of the water, and even make the educated experts look like they don&#39;t have a clue.  You could post it on any board or on every board.  Post different parts of it in different places under different names at different times.  Its a win/win situation.  Your story gets told, you show everyone else how dumb and wrong they are about you and your motivations, you get to stay anonymous, you have everybody reading your words and thoughts and pondering them, and you still keep them guessing.  You game?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
