<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4739"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 5:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why do you persist in sending info and packages to KAKE and WPD? Not only do they keep them a secret, but they lose them! Really! Where is your planning and foresight when it comes to communicating? More free floating anxiety will be generated if your letters are published in full. Again, get your just dues and send at least carbon copies to Tom. Everyone is looking forward to seeing you on the BTK trip this spring.  Please leave a drop for us. And get a new typewriter!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
