<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4806"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->pleasedeleteme<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 8:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Mr. Skillett, <BR> <BR>Oh! Oh! I get it.  <BR> <BR>Cereal = Serial! <BR> <BR>You clever devil. <BR> <BR>It’s almost as if Noel Coward has risen from the grave to become a homicidal maniac. <BR> <BR>Let’s take a closer look… <BR> <BR>Post Toasties® <BR> <BR>Could you mean… <BR> <BR>sPiTs at ote®os <BR> <BR>There are several other funny word games to play with these letters &#40;even some nasty ones&#41;!  <BR> <BR>And, it only took you 31 &#40;13!&#41; years to come up with it. <BR> <BR>The violent death of innocent women and children has never been more hilarious. <BR> <BR>You’re a reborn unknown comic. <BR> <BR>And now ladies and gentlemen, the BTK will present his final performance of the “Old Bag Trick”  -- on his own diseased head! <BR> <BR>Oh buddy… we’d eat that up with a spoon. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
