<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4875"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 5:02 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK -  <BR> <BR>I would like to know everything.  Truly everything.  You mentioned in a letter that it was a &#34;monster&#34;.  I would like to know if you still feel that way.  Do you think something occured early in your life that brought out this aspect?  The experts all say that there is a catalyst somewhere.  After all these years - I am sure you have delved deeply into your own psyche - and likely those of others, and by now, I think you may have a theory.  I would really like to know what that is. <BR> <BR>And I would like to know how you felt before, during and after the killings.  Were you ever frightened yourself?  Did you plan the crimes very far in advance?   <BR> <BR>And the victims - how did you choose them?  At ramdom?  On of my ideas &#40;probably wrong&#41; is that the women may have been rude to you in some way.  Demeaning.  But, I am usually pretty far off-base - so I&#39;m likely barking up the wrong tree. <BR> <BR>How were you able to keep everything quiet all these years?  Did you move?  Did you ever have the urge to tell? <BR> <BR>One of the biggest questions I have is whether you feel any real guilt?  Well, guilt is hard to define - do you ever feel any sorrow?   <BR> <BR>I may be wrong - but it seems that you stopped killing - at least here in Wichita.  If so - you defied the experts and their predictions.  That makes you an enigma. <BR> <BR>I know you won&#39;t get a chance to answer my questions, but I wanted to ask.  I&#39;m not here to judge or condemn - only to understand.   <BR> <BR>What makes one person choose to kill and another not?   <BR> <BR>If you get a chance to read this - thanks for listening.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4875-->
<!--Post: 4907--><!--Time: 1106804430-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4907"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Clair Voyant<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 26, 2005 - 9:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey B_ _T_ _ _K®, <BR> <BR>#7 is missing <BR> <BR>Overlooked <BR> <BR>Discarded <BR> <BR>Buried <BR> <BR>#7 was not planned <BR> <BR>Hasty <BR> <BR>Panicky <BR> <BR>Untidy <BR> <BR>#7 was a reaction <BR> <BR>A souvenir <BR> <BR>A revelation <BR> <BR>A gift <BR> <BR>#7 was your mistake <BR> <BR>I think <BR> <BR>I see <BR> <BR>I know <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
