<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5264"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Who&#39;sYourFloydW?<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 28, 2005 - 11:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Awakening <BR> <BR>Hey B_ _T_ _ _K®, <BR> <BR>Isn’t your motivational cancer or brain tumor or family tragedy nothing more than wishful thinking on “society’s” part? <BR> <BR>No. Your terminal disease is your mortality - - and it’s been exacerbated by the information age. <BR> <BR>I subscribe to the end game postulate that your reemergence is purely driven by public relations and a desire to remold your legacy in accordance with the changing times. <BR> <BR>Are you cleaning house to prepare for suicide? You know, that’s a common behavior among those planning to kick their own bucket. No. You’re letting go for a different reason. <BR> <BR>May we walk a mile in your moccasins? <BR> <BR>You fancy Nancy’s license in an entirely new way. You no longer squint at her through a pair of cheap readers from Dillon’s. You gaze at your prize in high resolution, enlarged 300% and illuminated on your monitor.  <BR> <BR>That is correct. <BR> <BR>Then you call up catchBTK.com to amuse yourself with Skov’s latest Googlings - - and to double check that it hasn’t hit too close to home. <BR> <BR>I mean, you really can’t afford not to, right? <BR> <BR>You click over to CrimeLibrary to read your biography - - again.  <BR> <BR>You fantasize about the books &#40;Oh, Truman why did you disappear?&#41; and the movie and your other true desire: <BR> <BR>–	The breeding that has begun and will continue to manifest after you’ve gone. <BR> <BR>STOP DAYDREAMING! <BR> <BR>Don’t forget to set the VCRs to capture the day’s newscasts. You’ll have your KAKE and Anita too! <BR> <BR>Everything is digitized and categorized, safe and hidden, available at your pleasure with a keystroke.  <BR> <BR>Are you in the clean room?  <BR> <BR>Good. Make a list, a map, a disguise, a date, a plan, an assemblage.  <BR> <BR>Check it. Check it again. Make certain. Is it safe? IS IT SAFE? <BR> <BR>Yes… it is…but, better check it again. <BR> <BR>Will it frighten? Check. <BR> <BR>Will it mislead? Check. <BR> <BR>Will it puzzle? Check. <BR> <BR>Society will see this. Check. <BR> <BR>But they won’t get to see that. Check. <BR> <BR>That is only for the WhooPteeDoos. Check <BR> <BR>Is it clean? Check. <BR> <BR>Check it again. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
