<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5664"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->TMBrown2004<!--/name--></b></a><br><!--field:posts--><!--/field--><!--field:registered--><!--/field--><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 7:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have a question about looking in between your clues... <BR>Do you want LE to subtract 2 from something?  You seem to reference this a lot in your clues... <BR>S Killett - Serial Killett &#40;T-2=r&#41; subtract 2 T&#39;s replace with r = Serial Killer - I also noticed a similar subtract 2 message in your Thomas Killman communication... Killman in the pre2004 Wichita directories list a single Killman - subtract two entries and you find Kilmer at an address that is 2 less than that used by you in your return address - 1684 - 2 = 1682. <BR>Is this the type of reading between the lines you wish people would do more of BTK?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
