<!--Post: 5698--><!--Time: 1107291826-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5698"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Flytodeb<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Flytodeb<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 01, 2005 - 1:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK! Do you read The New York Times? Look at page one of today&#39;s paper. Tuesday, February 1, 2005.  <BR>The article called &#34;Aneurysm Checks Urged in Older Men Who Have Smoked.&#34;  <BR>According to Dr. Ned Calonge, 65-75 year old men need to have an ultrasound screen test to see if they are developing a condition that could kill them in 10 minutes by bursting a major artery in the abdomen.  <BR>Wise up, man. You are a walking time bomb. Take your trophies and bag them up and turn yourself in. You not only will get special treatment in jail, but they will probably transfer you to a hospital setting because of your health. While you get expert medical attention you can be interviewed about your childhood, your adolescence, and your adult activities. Just do it. <BR>flytodeb<!--/Text--></td></tr>
