</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 5:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->To the killer: <BR>It is very frustrating posting here as I have no way of ever knowing if you do have any interest in reading it.  Most of us on this board &#40;self included&#41;must have too much spare time.  Maybe that is the only thing you and I have in common! <BR>But just in case you do get a chuckle from all of our attempts here, I freely admit one thing:  You have got more guts than I have.  I mean, with all the way Big Brother has come to pass, every single effort to communicate you make is literally putting your life out on a limb.  I would be terrified to mail anything from anywhere in WIchita.  The post office, with their automated readers, could be programmed to scan for specific names and addresses and sort that mail out for police.  I would be surprised if any post office did not have a camera hidden somewhere, and with webcams now the literal size of a peanut few businesses are going to be without a security cam somewhere.  Probably invisible.  And don&#39;t let some news statements fool you, practically anything purchased can be traced.  Some manufacturers are even wanting to put microchips in products which can be scanned at the register without anyone being the wiser.  Phone calls are definitely out, as with caller ID even private citizens have the number by the second ring.  Want to bet law enforcement can&#39;t get it way before the first ring is ever finished?  Not me. As for general surveillance, I have a picture of my house, by satellite, taken 10 years ago that shows my car is in the driveway. Note that is not the top secret limit of what could be done 10 years ago, just what the NSA is willing to admit to us now. <BR>Want to know the funniest thing about all this?  I&#39;m not even a paranoid kind of guy, I am actually kind of trusting!  Think how much worse it must be than I imagine!  Like I said, I would be too scared in your place to do anything again.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6015-->
<!--Post: 6025--><!--Time: 1107483412-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6025"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Medusa<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Medusa<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BTK - Give the contents of your most recent postcard here - what is your &#34;business message&#34; to WPD?  Tell us - also, take credit for one &#40;or more&#41; of your other murders here.  Come on, show some friggin balls and act like a man, not the little limp coward we all know you as.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6025-->
<!--Post: 6031--><!--Time: 1107485183-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6031"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Audreyamw<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Audreyamw<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->When the authorities find you &#40;and they will find you, El Puerco&#41;, I hope they spend lots of time picking over your brain so that we will know why you  really do the things you do.  They&#39;ll have all the time in the world to run all sorts of crazy tests on you.  You&#39;ll be locked up 23 hours a day &#40;at least&#41; in a tiny cell, with no time out of it except to exercise -- that would certainly be an improvement in your lifestyle, wouldn&#39;t it?    You might as well start making plans for your new  life on the inside, because I have a feeling it&#39;s going to be coming sooner rather than later.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6031-->
